{
  "name": "ENGINE1 | Canvas 02 | Smart Acknowledgment & Messaging | v1.0",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## CANVAS 02 · SMART ACKNOWLEDGMENT · v1.0\n**Input:** Canvas 01 durable outbox (`destination=canvas_02`).\n**Output:** consented email acknowledged through Resend; provider ID, delivery status, and audit records stored in PostgreSQL.\n\n**No direct Canvas 01 webhook dependency.** A 1-minute worker claims one due job; an independent 15-minute worker checks delivery by provider ID. A manual trigger makes setup testing possible before publication.\n\n**Safety:** global kill switch + explicit email consent + contact opt-out + exact recipient allowlist + daily cap + quiet hours. Distinct repeat inquiries are eligible; event-key replays produce no new jobs.",
        "height": 370,
        "width": 650,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "f29bbd55-606a-4965-8279-fcd6d432d8ff",
      "name": "README · Canvas 02 / behavior",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        640,
        16
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## REQUIRED BEFORE SENDING\n1. Backup database; apply `ENGINE1_Canvas02_Required_Migration_v1.0.sql` as one transaction.\n2. Assign PostgreSQL credential to all B/P database nodes.\n3. Assign existing **Resend Header Auth credential** to both HTTP nodes; it must send `Authorization: Bearer ...`. **Never insert tokens into workflow JSON.**\n4. Add only your owned/approved email address to `c02_demo_email_allowlist` in PostgreSQL.\n5. Keep `messaging_kill_switch=true` until controlled tests. An eligible lead needs `email_consent:true` from Canvas 01. Test sender `onboarding@resend.dev` generally supports account-owned recipient only.\n6. Pingram remains deferred because its API currently returns 403; SMS does **not** send.",
        "height": 354,
        "width": 544,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "af16c36f-5bf0-417f-b156-8321ae03924c",
      "name": "README · Prerequisites, setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2640,
        704
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## POLICY / RECOVERY\nLocal time: **Asia/Karachi 21:00–09:00** (read from `system_state`).\n`c02_email_quiet_mode=after_hours` sends permitted email immediately with after-hours copy; `defer` holds to next 09:00. SMS never sends until Pingram API is repaired.\n\nRetries: 429/5xx (or Resend concurrent idempotency conflict) with the SAME frozen payload and idempotency key, max 3 sends and <=20h from first attempt. Network timeout / expired in-flight lease = **unknown; manual reconciliation**, not blind resend. An incident is queued for Canvas 06. Failed delivery is also queued for Canvas 06 (no unsafe automatic second send).",
        "height": 209,
        "width": 1038,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "ff455edf-fb8d-4b9e-ade3-ff7ce9f0d787",
      "name": "README · Quiet hours and durable retries",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1328,
        -112
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## TEST GATES (BEFORE PUBLISHING)\n1. Kill switch ON: manual run -> `paused_kill_switch`; no send.\n2. Consent false: distinct lead -> `skipped_no_consent`; no provider request.\n3. Recipient not allowlisted: `deferred_allowlist`; no send.\n4. Approved owned recipient + email consent: POST once; `accepted` with provider ID.\n5. Manual run again: no duplicate send.\n6. Genuine repeat: new lead ID, same contact, independent allowed acknowledgment.\n7. Quiet mode `defer`: waits until local 09:00 (test via DB fixtures, not arbitrary wall-clock changes).\n8. Simulate provider 429/5xx, 401/403, delivery failed, and uncertain timeout on disposable test fixtures. Do not turn on Pingram.",
        "height": 274,
        "width": 864,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "f2387556-2869-4ddb-81a6-a8c09cb12e18",
      "name": "README · Test matrix",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
